  "title": "Reopened Investigation into Ann Widdecombe's Murder and Attempted Burglary",
  "summary": "The Guardian and Financial Times report that the police are reopening an investigation into Ann Widdecombe's murder, which was previously dismissed, and that counter-terrorism officers identified relevant information missed during an investigation into an attempted burglary in Greater London. South Korea's police will re-examine 310,000 missing person cases after a scandal involving an officer who falsified records to close files on two people who were later found dead. The government has ordered an investigation into the police handling of the cases and plans to reform criminal justice to address systemic issues.",
